# Generated reports / analyses / plugin design proposals (committed history kept; new files ignored)
reports/
**/_design/
**/_analysis/
**/_research/
**/_proposals/
*-design-spec.md
*-analysis-report.md

# Session handoffs — LOCAL-ONLY since 2026-08-17 (user decision via /save).
# Previously committed for cross-machine visibility, but the landing-flow gate
# makes per-session commits impractical (five sessions of permanent dirty tree).
# Trade-off accepted: handoffs are per-machine local records; cross-machine
# context restore relies on git-tracked guides + auto-memory instead.
.artibot/HANDOFF.md
.artibot/handoffs/
# /split run state (plan.json, run.json, list-agents.txt, locks/, per-limb brief.md in
# worktrees) — per-machine local records, never committed (commands/split.md "plan" step 7).
.artibot/split/

# Session work products written at the repo root (reports, proposals, exported
# docs). Same local-only rationale as the handoffs above: they are per-session
# records, not repo state. Root-anchored so it cannot swallow a future
# `plugins/*/artifacts/` that a build step legitimately tracks.
# Concrete reason it is here: during the v4.49.0 release this directory sat
# untracked and un-ignored, one `git add -A` away from shipping a .docx.
/artifacts/

# Auto-generated per-session timeline log — hooks rewrite it every session,
# so it only adds dirty-tree noise to git status / /save. Read from the working
# tree by hooks (session-notes.js, dev-verify-gate.js, pr-description-builder.js);
# no consumer requires it to be git-tracked. Not cross-machine state (unlike HANDOFF.md).
.artibot/SESSION-NOTES.md

# Ambient Conversation Ledger — per-session denoised conversation archive.
# Local-only (DATA POLICY): contains verbatim user/assistant conversation text
# (secret-redacted, but still private). NEVER commit — keep out of git entirely.
# `**/` so it matches whether the hook's projectRoot is the repo root or a
# nested cwd (e.g. plugins/artibot/.artibot/ledger/ during in-repo dev).
**/.artibot/ledger/

# /scorecard snapshot store — per-machine progress history appended by
# lib/planning/scorecard.js. Same local-only rationale as SESSION-NOTES.md:
# it is a record of what one operator measured in one session, not repo state,
# and it grows on every /scorecard run. Named as a single file rather than
# `.artibot/` so it cannot swallow the seven tracked files in that directory
# (guides/, failure-patterns.json, the backlog notes).
.artibot/scorecard.json

# Claude Code plan-mode ephemeral state — machine-local absolute paths, stale
# across sessions. Never commit.
.plan-state.json
